###
# TASK 3: Concurrent WebSocket Real-Time Communication Hub
# REST Microservice HTTP Endpoints Specification
###

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. System Health & Infrastructure Metrics
# Inspects uptime, memory consumption, WebSocket connections, Redis status, and persistent file logger status.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. List All Active Channels
# Returns all default and dynamically registered channels with their real-time subscriber counts.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Get Active Members of a Specific Channel
# Queries Redis sets to return full profiles of all active users inside #tech
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/tech/users
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Get Active Members of General Channel
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/general/users
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. List All Active Users Cached in Redis
# Fetches all online users currently cached inside the Redis memory database.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/active
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. Query Persistent Transaction Audit Logs (Latest 50)
# Reads transaction timestamps and metadata directly from the append-only persistent file store.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/logs/transactions?limit=50
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Filter Persistent Audit Logs by Event Type
# Filters transactions for MESSAGE_SENT events
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/logs/transactions?event=MESSAGE_SENT&limit=25
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Filter Persistent Audit Logs by Target Channel
# Filters transactions for messages sent to #general
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/logs/transactions?channel=general&limit=20
Accept: application/json

###

### 9. Persistent File Store Logger Statistics
# Retrieves metrics on total logged transactions, pending buffer size, and active log file paths.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/logs/stats
Accept: application/json
